# GoldenEye 007 PC Port — @VERSION@ (alpha)

A native PC port of the original Nintendo 64 *GoldenEye 007*, compiled from the
[GoldenEye 007 decompilation](https://github.com/n64decomp/007).

> **Very early research alpha — not a playable game.**
> The intro and menus render and all 21 solo missions load, but there is
> **no audio**, some 3D models and text are broken, ladders don't work yet
> (and can block progression on some levels), and you should expect crashes and
> glitches past the level intro. This is a technical demo of the porting work.
>
> If you just want to *play* GoldenEye on PC, use one of the Xbox 360
> recompilation projects instead — see the project page.

Project & source: <https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port>

---

## 1. You must supply your own ROM

This package contains **no Nintendo code and no game data**. You need a
*GoldenEye 007* Nintendo 64 ROM that **you legally own**, big-endian `.z64`,
NTSC-U (US):

| ROM filename | SHA-1 |
|---|---|
| `ge007.ntsc-final.z64` | `abe01e4aeb033b6c0836819f549c791b26cfde83` |

Only the US ROM is supported in this alpha.

## 2. Run

1. Unzip this folder anywhere.
2. Make a `data` folder next to `ge007.x86_64.exe`.
3. Copy your ROM into it, named exactly: `data\ge007.ntsc-final.z64`
4. Run `ge007.x86_64.exe` **from this folder**.

Configuration is written to `ge007.ini` on first run.

> If the game exits immediately reporting missing data, your ROM's assets need
> the one-time extraction step described under "Building" in the project README
> — the alpha binary expects the same asset layout a source build produces.

## 3. Controls (defaults)

| Action | Keyboard / mouse |
|---|---|
| Move / strafe | `W` `A` `S` `D` / arrows |
| Aim / look | mouse |
| Fire | left mouse / `LCtrl` |
| Aim mode | right mouse / `LShift` |
| Use / accept | `Space` / `E` |
| Reload / cancel | `R` / `F` |
| Start | `Enter` / `Tab` |

Mouse sensitivity and Y-inversion are in the `[Input]` section of `ge007.ini`.

